om_owner",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":11,"beg":{"line":250,"col":4},"end":{"line":286,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":"pub fn from_owner<T>(owner: T) -> Self\n    where\n        T: AsRef<[u8]> + Send + 'static,\n    {\n        // Safety & Miri:\n        // The ownership of `owner` is first transferred to the `Owned` wrapper and `Bytes` object.\n        // This ensures that the owner is pinned in memory, allowing us to call `.as_ref()` safely\n        // since the lifetime of the owner is controlled by the lifetime of the new `Bytes` object,\n        // and the lifetime of the resulting borrowed `&[u8]` matches that of the owner.\n        // Note that this remains safe so long as we only call `.as_ref()` once.\n        //\n        // There are some additional special considerations here:\n        //   * We rely on Bytes's Drop impl to clean up memory should `.as_ref()` panic.\n        //   * Setting the `ptr` and `len` on the bytes object last (after moving the owner to\n        //     Bytes) allows Miri checks to pass since it avoids obtaining the `&[u8]` slice\n        //     from a stack-owned Box.\n        // More details on this: https://github.com/tokio-rs/bytes/pull/742/#discussion_r1813375863\n        //                  and: https://github.com/tokio-rs/bytes/pull/742/#discussion_r1813316032\n\n        let owned = Box::into_raw(Box::new(Owned {\n            ref_cnt: AtomicUsize::new(1),\n            owner,\n        }));\n\n        let mut ret = Bytes {\n            ptr: NonNull::dangling().as_ptr(),\n            len: 0,\n            data: AtomicPtr::new(owned.cast()),\n            vtable: &Owned::<T>::VTABLE,\n        };\n\n        let buf = unsafe { &*owned }.owner.as_ref();\n        ret.ptr = buf.as_ptr();\n        ret.len = buf.len();\n\n        ret\n    }","attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Create [Bytes] with a buffer whose lifetime is controlled"},{"DocComment":" via an explicit owner."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" A common use case is to zero-copy construct from mapped memory."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" # struct File;"},{"DocComment":" #"},{"DocComment":" # impl File {"},{"DocComment":" #     pub fn open(_: &str) -> Result<Self, ()> {"},{"DocComment":" #         Ok(Self)"},{"DocComment":" #     }"},{"DocComment":" # }"},{"DocComment":" #"},{"DocComment":" # mod memmap2 {"},{"DocComment":" #     pub struct Mmap;"},{"DocComment":" #"},{"DocComment":" #     impl Mmap {"},{"DocComment":" #         pub unsafe fn map(_file: &super::File) -> Result<Self, ()> {"},{"DocComment":" #             Ok(Self)"},{"DocComment":" #         }"},{"DocComment":" #     }"},{"DocComment":" #"},{"DocComment":" #     impl AsRef<[u8]> for Mmap {"},{"DocComment":" #         fn as_ref(&self) -> &[u8] {"},{"DocComment":" #             b\"buf\""},{"DocComment":" #         }"},{"DocComment":" #     }"},{"DocComment":" # }"},{"DocComment":" use bytes::Bytes;"},{"DocComment":" use memmap2::Mmap;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # fn main() -> Result<(), ()> {"},{"DocComment":" let file = File::open(\"upload_bundle.tar.gz\")?;"},{"DocComment":" let mmap = unsafe { Mmap::map(&file) }?;"},{"DocComment":" let b = Bytes::from_owner(mmap);"},{"DocComment":" # Ok(())"},{"DocComment":" # }"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The `owner` will be transferred to the constructed [Bytes] object, which"},{"DocComment":" will ensure it is dropped once all remaining clones of the constructed"},{"DocComment":" object are dropped. The owner will then be responsible for dropping the"},{"DocComment":" specified region of memory as part of its [Drop] implementation."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Note that converting [Bytes] constructed from an owner into a [BytesMut]"},{"DocComment":" will always create a deep copy of the buffer into newly allocated memory."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":true,"started_from":true,"is_extern":false,"